Sval: let Sval decide the file pickers and downloads of an agent's tab

A page in a tab an agent controls may open no file picker, and its downloads
are decided by a per-site permission, saved with no dialog and never opened.
Gecko makes both in the parent with no chrome hook of its own: a picker from
the @mozilla.org/filepicker;1 contract in FilePickerParent::RecvOpen, a
download's dialog and transfer from @mozilla.org/helperapplauncherdialog;1
and @mozilla.org/transfer;1 in nsExternalAppHandler. Standing a component in
front of those contracts puts Sval in every picker and download, and fights
whatever else registers over them, such as a test's mock. So these ask
Sval's nsISvalAgentFiles first, through the helpers in Sval's SvalAgentFiles.h,
which knows which tabs an agent controls: a refused picker is never made and
comes back cancelled, and Sval may hand out its own dialog and transfer.
Every other tab's pickers and downloads go to Firefox's components as
before.

diff --git a/dom/ipc/FilePickerParent.cpp b/dom/ipc/FilePickerParent.cpp
index 97f8ee46a5..0c9401b3ab 100644
--- a/dom/ipc/FilePickerParent.cpp
+++ b/dom/ipc/FilePickerParent.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 #include "FilePickerParent.h"
 
+#include "mozilla/SvalAgentFiles.h"
 #include "mozilla/dom/BrowserParent.h"
 #include "mozilla/dom/CanonicalBrowsingContext.h"
 #include "mozilla/dom/ContentParent.h"
@@ -276,7 +277,9 @@ mozilla::ipc::IPCResult FilePickerParent::RecvOpen(
     nsTArray<nsString>&& aRawFilters, const nsString& aDisplayDirectory,
     const nsString& aDisplaySpecialDirectory, const nsString& aOkButtonLabel,
     const nsIFilePicker::CaptureTarget& aCapture) {
-  if (!CreateFilePicker()) {
+  // Sval: no picker is made for a page in a tab an agent controls.
+  if (mozilla::sval::RefusesFilePicker(mBrowsingContext) ||
+      !CreateFilePicker()) {
     (void)Send__delete__(this, void_t(), nsIFilePicker::returnCancel);
     return IPC_OK();
   }
